#doc (Manual) "The bottom of F0" =>

The downsets of $`t_1, \ldots, t_5` are computed exactly, and seven covers read
off them: $`F_0` is not dense.  The results are in `wip/f0Covers.lean`.

:::f0Figure "bottom" (width := "0.42")
The bottom of $`F_0`: the six elements of $`{\downarrow}t_5`, each labelled by its
defining formula ($`t_4` is $`\lnot\lnot\bigcirc\bot` up to $`\dashv\vdash`), and
the seven covers $`u \lessdot v`, each PROVED (`cover_0_1`, …, `cover_4_5`,
{srcLink}`cover_0_1`).  The nodes are the list `D5_list` and the lines the
cover theorems, read off their types by `tools/F0/FigureData.lean`.
:::

Below $`\lnot\bigcirc\bot` there is only $`\bot`, and every other variable-free
formula lies above $`\bigcirc\bot`:

$$`F_0 = \{\bot, \lnot\bigcirc\bot\} \cup {\uparrow}\bigcirc\bot.`

PROVED, from the table for $`{\downarrow}t_2` and the dichotomy of Section 2.

