A cover $`u \lessdot v` follows from a table for $`{\downarrow}v` containing $`u`
once no other member lies strictly between.  In the $`\bigcirc`-free instance
the same seven covers are those of the Rieger–Nishimura ladder (`covers9_eq`,
decided by `decide`); the tables add that no formula with $`\bigcirc` falls into
the seven intervals.

